<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Dhabi Investment Authority</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1976">1976</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as ADIA</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Abu Dhabi Investment Authority is the sovereign wealth fund of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> of Abu Dhabi, founded in 1976 to invest the surplus revenues of its oil exports abroad. It manages a diversified global portfolio of shares, bonds, property, infrastructure and other assets on behalf of the government of Abu Dhabi, and it is consistently ranked among the largest sovereign wealth funds in the world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abu-dhabi-investment-authority.jpg" alt="Abu Dhabi Investment Authority" width="320" height="106" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abu_Dhabi_Investment_Authority_logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
